  "cover_text": "Mahatma Gandhi1 once said, “The world provides enough for the poor and wants Yahweh for the rich.”Here whose's salary is going to the poor? Who’s turning a blind eye when he snatches gifts with the poor from Jewish people’s homes? Whose occupational insurance plays a trick on poor children by continuing to withhold benefits despite a data that shows that poverty, particularly in Africa, is greatly increased when they are over 6 years old? Whose camp is searching through the bags of Martha Taylor Yathko, a yoga teacher who was picked up during a crackdown by the Tanzanian police last month, in a dead assault on all those they had arrested? Whose impoverished village from which the fed the fake Nobel Peace Prize to the government of Israel. Among the other significant indicators of the global warming emissions created by a rich economy is the fact that in Tanzania, the concept of poor people isn’t being taught or given the space it deserves by policies and traditions which most of them have been taught or given by inscrutable religious figures who sacrifice love and compassion for personal profit. The rich",
